Falsifies `system_tests::user::live_swap_tests::a_client_of_the_stable_rendezvous_cannot_become_its_server`.

Architecture: aarch64

The patch deletes the `READ` check on `Rendezvous::RECEIVE_CAP` in
`syscall::rendezvous::rendezvous_receive_capability`, the gate this test exists for (the kernel-side
twin's record deletes `RECEIVE`'s; one test carries one patch). Until milestone 800 (a non-Anthropic
model attacks the confinement claim) reshaped the fixture, this defect could not turn the test red:
a let-open `RECEIVE_CAP` found an empty queue and blocked, and the run died at the 60-second
watchdog instead of at the assertion (measured 2026-09-16, milestone 305 (the six kernel confinement
rows get a falsification a machine can replay)). The operator now retires the last receiver first
and a plant (`swap_boundary_witness`'s `ROLE_PLANT`) parks `hot_swap_contract::PLANT_MARKER` on the endpoint, so the
broken gate returns that word and the assertion fires: `error -1394018833` is `-PLANT_MARKER`.

Expected to fail: `assert_eq!` "a client of the stable rendezvous received on it (or was refused
for the wrong reason)", with `left: 18446744072315532783` (the negated marker). Replayed red at
exactly that assertion on aarch64 on 2026-10-07 (UTC) by the milestone 800 lane, the pass's fourth.

Re-cut on 2026-10-12 (UTC) by lane maintainer/long-function-paydown-invoke, when the rendezvous
arms of `syscall::invoke` moved to `kernel/src/syscall/rendezvous.rs` for milestone 888 (a ratchet
on function length); the defect is unchanged. Replayed red at the same assertion on aarch64 that
day.

